================================================================================================
D5 -- THE g_ext SYSTEMATIC AND THE CLOSED-FORM SHAPE ROUTE (best case for
      the degeneracy-breaking hypothesis)
================================================================================================
  The ONLY C-free route to a0: the shape's transition location measures g_extN
  in PHYSICAL units; the framework's own inversion then gives a0 with NO
  reference to C:      a0 = (g_ext,obs^2 - g_extN^2)/g_extN.
  Closed-form log-derivatives (u = g_extN/a0, exact):
      d ln a0 / d ln g_extN   = -(2u + 1)
      d ln a0 / d ln g_ext,obs = +2(u + 1)
  [canonical] u = 1.4643: lever on g_extN = -3.929, on g_ext,obs = +4.929  (both VERIFIED numerically)
           maximal shape measurement of the transition: sigma(ln g_extN) = 62.7%  (marginalizing the amplitude C*a0)
           -> sigma(ln a0) from the shape alone = 246% ; with a 2.4% g_ext,obs prior = 247%
  [ALT] u = 1.1510: lever on g_extN = -3.302, on g_ext,obs = +4.302  (both VERIFIED numerically)
           maximal shape measurement of the transition: sigma(ln g_extN) = 51.6%  (marginalizing the amplitude C*a0)
           -> sigma(ln a0) from the shape alone = 170% ; with a 2.4% g_ext,obs prior = 171%
  FROZEN g_ext CONVENTION SPREAD: 1.778e-10 vs 2.078e-10 = 15.6% in ln g_ext,obs
      through the +4.93 lever that is 77% on a0 by the shape route,
      and 14% on a0 by the amplitude route (the two frozen g_ext values move the MI asymptote 1.1015 -> 1.0854).
  READING: the shape route is C-FREE (a genuine degeneracy break) but the
  transition-location lever AMPLIFIES errors ~3.3-3.9x, and the frozen g_ext
  convention spread alone is a ~60-80% a0 systematic through it.  It is the
  weakest of the three routes, not the rescue.

  Additional non-averaging WB systematic (task item 1, honestly quantified):
  photometric masses. vtilde ~ M^(-1/2) and the g_N axis ~ M, so a COHERENT
  mass-scale offset d lnM shifts gamma by -d lnM/2 plus a transition shift.
      global M-L offset 2% -> d gamma = -0.0100 -> sigma(ln a0) = 9%  (amplitude route)
      global M-L offset 3% -> d gamma = -0.0150 -> sigma(ln a0) = 13%  (amplitude route)
      global M-L offset 5% -> d gamma = -0.0250 -> sigma(ln a0) = 22%  (amplitude route)
  So WB masses are NOT systematic-free: a 3% coherent main-sequence M-L offset
  already costs ~13% in a0 -- MORE than the ENTIRE dwarf 11.0% floor.
  Mass-lever comparison, computed: dwarf a0-line d ln a0/d ln Upsilon = 0.0810/0.2303 = 0.35;
  WB d ln a0/d ln M = 0.5/0.1133 = 4.41  ->  the WB mass lever is
  12.5x STEEPER.  Main-sequence M-L models ARE tighter than galaxy
  Upsilon (~2-5% vs 0.10 dex = 23%), but the steeper lever cancels most of
  that advantage.  The prior claim that WB carries 'no Upsilon at all' is
  CORRECTED here, not upheld: the axis is different, the magnitude is not.

================================================================================================
D6 -- THE JOINT WITH THE DWARF a0-LINE: WHAT WOULD WB HAVE TO DELIVER?
================================================================================================
  3-sigma separation of canonical from the 1.13-1.20e-10 cluster needs a
  joint sigma(ln a0) <= 6.31%.
  Given the dwarf floor 11.0% (GLS-committed), WB must deliver sigma(ln a0) <= 7.71%
  Given the dwarf floor 11.6% (SPARC-alone stack), WB must deliver <= 7.52%
  i.e. WB would have to be a TIGHTER a0 measurement than the dwarf line is,
  not merely a comparable one.  Via the ASYMPTOTE-ONLY route that requires
  sigma(gamma) <= 0.0087 -- vs the frozen sigma_sys allowance alone = 0.0200 (2.3x too
  large) and sigma_tot = 0.0277 (3.2x too large).  The FULL-CURVE route below does
  better than that and is the one the ladder uses.

  Joint ladder (quadrature; WB and dwarf systematics ARE orthogonal, so this
  IS the fair combination -- the orthogonality hypothesis is fully granted).
  WB sigmas are the FULL-CURVE Fisher numbers from the D3b ladder, i.e. the
  best (not the worst) route available at each level of knowledge.
  WB scenario                                                      s_WB    joint  3sig?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A. lambda+g_ext EXACT, sigma_sys ZEROED (counterfactual best)    10.0%    7.40%     no
  B. A + 3% coherent photometric M-L offset                       16.6%    9.17%     no
  C. lambda EXACT, g_ext 2.4% prior, sigma_sys ZEROED             10.2%    7.47%     no
  D. sigma_sys as a per-bin floor, lambda+g_ext EXACT             13.3%    8.47%     no
  E. frozen sigma_sys as a lambda prior + g_ext 2.4% (realistic)    21.0%    9.74%     no
  F. E + 3% coherent photometric M-L offset                       24.8%   10.06%     no
  G. banked MI band 1.0508-1.1015 as the prescription prior       16.9%    9.22%     no
  H. full MI-to-MG bracket 1.0508-1.1389 as the prior             25.3%   10.09%     no
  I. no prescription knowledge (lambda free)                     147.1%   10.97%     no
  J. C-free transition-location route only (D5)                  246.6%   10.99%     no
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dwarf-alone reference: 11.00%   target 6.31%   WB must beat 7.71% for the joint to reach it
  Rows G/H use uniform-bracket sigmas (width/sqrt12) so the banked theory
  bracket is NOT inflated beyond a fair reading.
  BEST joint on the whole ladder = 7.40% (still short of 6.31%); shortfall factor 1.17x.
  Statistical-only N requirement, in the COUNTERFACTUAL best case (row A: no
  systematics at all, prescription and g_ext exact): sigma scales as 1/sqrt(N),
  so reaching the 7.71% WB budget needs N ~ 50,456 pairs vs the 30,000 the frozen
  pre-registration forecasts -- and that row is the one that zeroes the very
  systematics the frozen sigma_sys allowance exists to cover.

================================================================================================
D7 -- WHAT WB *CAN* DO (the honest positive, reported symmetrically)
================================================================================================
  Run the inference BACKWARDS: fix a0 from the dwarf a0-line and ask what the
  same DR4 gamma measurement then determines.
  [canonical] sigma(ln lambda) = 10.6% stat, 22.4% with the frozen sigma_sys
  [ALT] sigma(ln lambda) = 8.5% stat, 21.5% with the frozen sigma_sys
  So DR4 WB, with a0 supplied externally, constrains the nu+EFE PRESCRIPTION
  (the MI-vs-MG / dilution axis) to ~15-25% -- which is exactly what the
  frozen pre-registration already claims: 'DR4 gamma_v constrains the nu+EFE
  prescription, NOT the value a0 = 9.36e-11.'  That is a real deliverable; it
  is just NOT an a0 amplitude, so it cannot enter the a0 joint.
  It also inherits the frozen MI-vs-MG verdict: separating 1.09 from 1.137 at
  3 sigma needs N ~ 45,000 AND sigma_sys < 0.01 -- pre-declared likely
  UNDECIDABLE in DR4.

================================================================================================
VERDICT (degeneracy test; a manufactured win and a manufactured deficit are
         penalized equally)
================================================================================================
  1. NO-EFE READING (L1, Milgrom arXiv:2503.07106 -- the largest-signal WB
     reading): the a0-C degeneracy is EXACT.  d gamma/d lnC and d gamma/d ln a0
     are identical to machine precision (2.2e-12), the 2x2 Fisher determinant is
     2.39e-13, and the null direction is the C*a0 = const ray.  The
     gamma(separation) SHAPE is a RIGID one-parameter family in C*a0 and adds
     ZERO breaking.  a0's amplitude is STRICTLY unmeasurable here.
  2. EFE READINGS (L2/L3): the second scale g_extN lifts the EXACT degeneracy,
     but only weakly -- the a0 and prescription derivative vectors are nearly
     parallel (weighted cos = 0.9977 for the framework's own MI-EFE law),
     inflating sigma(ln a0) by x14.7.  SO: THE SHAPE DOES NOT BREAK THE
     a0-C DEGENERACY.  It breaks the AMPLITUDE-vs-TRANSITION degeneracy, which
     is a different (and insufficient) thing.
     CONFIRMED NON-LINEARLY (D3d, not just by Fisher): with the prescription
     strength free, the PROFILE chi2 in a0 is FLAT -- dchi2<=1 spans
     [0.10, 3.08] x a0_true even when the model is the TRUE law, and it
     runs off a factor-10 grid.  And MG data fitted with the MI law gives
     chi2_min = 1.61 on 8 bins at a0_hat = 9.5 x a0_true: the two
     prescriptions are SHAPE-INDISTINGUISHABLE at DR4 precision, so mis-picking
     one biases a0 by up to an ORDER OF MAGNITUDE with no chi2 penalty.
  3. WHAT DOES BREAK, AND BY HOW MUCH (stated in the framework's favour first):
     the framework's OWN inversion g_extN(a0, g_ext,obs) does supply a second,
     a0-dependent scale, so with the prescription EXACT and g_ext EXACT the full
     curve formally measures a0 at 10.0% -- genuinely BETTER than the
     asymptote-only route (17%), and comparable to the dwarf 11.0% floor.
     That is the strongest honest form of the shape-breaks-it hypothesis and it
     is granted in full.  It still fails the joint, on arithmetic:
       the joint needs WB <= 7.71% -- TIGHTER than the dwarf floor itself,
       because 1/6.31^2 - 1/11.0^2 leaves only that much room.
       best joint anywhere on the ladder = 7.40%, i.e. 1.17x short.
       and even that row needs N ~ 50,456 pairs, not the 30,000 forecast.
  4. THE REALISTIC ROWS ARE MUCH WORSE, and the reasons are all banked, not
     invented: the frozen sigma_sys = 0.02 read as a coherent prescription
     offset gives 21%; the banked MI band 1.0508-1.1015 gives 17%;
     the full MI-to-MG bracket 1.0508-1.1389 is a factor-3.11 range in C_eff,
     i.e. ~78% in a0 from THEORY ALONE.  A 3% coherent photometric
     M-L offset costs 13% (WB masses are NOT systematic-free).  And
     contamination adds a ONE-SIDED upward bias worth +91% in a0 at the
     DR3 dry-run level -- which is exactly why gamma=1.205 is evidence for
     nothing.  No row on the ladder reaches 3 sigma in the joint.
  5. VERDICT: NO -- WB cannot supply a usable a0 AMPLITUDE for the joint.
     * In the no-EFE reading it supplies ONLY the product C*a0 (exact degeneracy).
     * In the EFE readings it supplies a0 only after the prescription is FIXED,
       and the framework's MI completion is banked as UNWRITTEN, so the
       prescription bracket is a real, non-optional 45-78% a0 uncertainty.
     * Even granting a fixed prescription, exact g_ext, and full orthogonality of
       WB-vs-dwarf systematics, the joint reaches 7.40%, not 6.31%.
     So the ORTHOGONALITY PREMISE OF THE HYPOTHESIS IS CORRECT and irrelevant:
     the blocker is not shared systematics, it is that a0 and the two-body /
     prescription coefficient enter the wide-binary observable in the same
     combination.  This is a DEGENERACY wall.  More pairs, tighter screens and
     DR4's new NSS cut do not touch it.
  6. WHAT WOULD CHANGE THIS (open doors, stated because they exist): (i) a
     WRITTEN MI completion that FIXES C_eff from first principles -- WB then
     becomes a real if weak ~13% a0 datum (joint 8.47%), still short but no
     longer degenerate; (ii) an independent g_ext,obs at ~1% (the two FROZEN
     conventions differ by 16%) to make the C-free transition-location route
     usable; (iii) DR4 radial velocities removing the deprojection prior-
     sensitivity the banked wb_mond_orbit_mc.py flagged; (iv) attacking the
     DWARF side instead -- the estimator-choice term is 30% of that variance and
     is an ANALYSIS ambiguity, not a data limitation.  None closed; none in hand.
  NOT 'theory closed'.  The framework's a0 amplitude is simply not what a wide-
  binary gamma measures.

